00 - Intro

What is the Web?
- The World Wide Web is a collection of information accessible throught the Internet.
- Computers connected to the web are called a client to server relationship.


HTTP
- Web clients and server communicate over the HTTP protocol.
- The client initiates by sending an HTTP request messagge to the server, then passes a HTTP response to the client..
- The server responds with an HTTP response message, through the server to the client.


Client Request
- EX: Using a URL in a browser and searching it.
- URL (Uniform Resource Locator): An identifier for the location of a document.
- Scheme: Indicates the protocol that the browser must utilize to request the resource.
- Domain Name: Indicates which Web server is being requested.
- Port Number: Indicates which application on the server willl receive the message.
- Path: Direction to the resource on the Web server.

http - Scheme
www.example.com - Domain Name
80 - Port
/path/to/myfile.html - Path to the file

http://www.example.com:80/path/to/myfile.html


Where is the server?
- Domain name is not an IP address.
- Instead, to identify the server location, you request the IP address from Domain Name Service (DNS).

 Web            --> Domain Name -->     DNS
Client          <-- IP Address <--


- Send an HTTP request to the web server identifies by the IP address.
- Web server locates the resource and sends a response.
- Upon receiving the response, the browser parses the information and renders the page.

